  "name": "Faith and Belief",
  "publisher": "Initiative",
  "description": "For what you believe, and everyone who believes something else.",
  "long_description": "Eleven of them, one each, the same size on the same disc, in no order that means anything: Christian, Muslim, Jewish, Hindu, Buddhist, Sikh, Taoist, Bahá'í, Jain, Shinto and Wiccan. The banners and the frames are deliberately not any one of them — a street where seven kinds of roof stand next to each other, a night when everybody's lamps are lit, five doorways all standing open, and two rings: eleven symbols going round together, or two strands over and under the whole way. Wear yours. Or wear the street.",
